WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.233
Let's see how to install and use Google Cloud Tools extension

00:00:02.233 --> 00:00:03.700
for Visual Studio

00:00:04.166 --> 00:00:07.166
To install, go to tools, then extensions and updates in Visual Studio

00:00:07.166 --> 00:00:10.166
Click on online and search for Google Cloud Platform extension

00:00:10.166 --> 00:00:13.166
Once installed, it will show up under installed section

00:00:13.166 --> 00:00:16.166
You can find the extension under Tools

00:00:16.166 --> 00:00:19.166
and Google Cloud Tools. Before we can use the extension,

00:00:19.166 --> 00:00:22.166
we need to add our account, so let's do that

00:00:28.166 --> 00:00:31.166
Let's open Google Cloud Explorer and select our project from the list

00:00:34.166 --> 00:00:37.166
Under Compute Engine, you can see status

00:00:37.166 --> 00:00:40.166
or create a new Windows or Linux Compute Engine instance

00:00:40.166 --> 00:00:43.166
You can also see different

00:00:43.166 --> 00:00:46.166
regions/zones and perform some operations on instances in those regions 

00:00:49.166 --> 00:00:51.133
Under Cloud Storage, you can see the list of buckets

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:54.500
browse them by going to Cloud Console

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:57.500
Under Cloud SQL, you can see Cloud SQL instances 

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:59.733
and create data connections to them. Thanks for watching!

